  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "1. Weight and activation tiles sit in HBM3, 8 stacks surrounding the 4 IODs.",
      "focus": ["hbm-dram-west", "hbm-dram-east", "hbm-base-west", "hbm-base-east"],
      "dot": "hbm-dram-west",
      "explode": 0.6,
      "drill": null,
      "stage": "hbm"
    },
    {
      "text": "2. A memory controller in the IOD reads its local HBM3 stack.",
      "focus": ["mc-iod0"],
      "dot": "mc-iod0",
      "stage": "memory-controller"
    },
    {
      "text": "3. If the tile lives in another IOD's HBM, Infinity Fabric AP carries it across the package — coherent across all 4 IODs, not just one bridge.",
      "focus": ["infinity-fabric-link"],
      "dot": "infinity-fabric-link",
      "stage": "die-to-die"
    },
    {
      "text": "4. The tile lands in this IOD's slice of the 256 MB Infinity Cache.",
      "focus": ["icache-0"],
      "dot": "icache-0",
      "stage": "infinity-cache"
    },
    {
      "text": "5. The XCD stacked above pulls the tile into its own 4 MB L2 cache.",
      "focus": ["l2-xcd"],
      "dot": "l2-xcd",
      "drill": "xcd-detail",
      "stage": "l2"
    },
    {
      "text": "6. A wavefront copies the operand tile from L2 into the CU's 64 KB LDS.",
      "focus": ["lds"],
      "dot": "lds",
      "drill": "cu-detail",
      "stage": "shared-memory"
    },
    {
      "text": "7. The wavefront issues a v_mfma instruction: the CU's 4 Matrix Cores multiply the tile (e.g. in FP8).",
      "focus": ["matrix-core"],
      "dot": "matrix-core",
      "drill": "cu-detail",
      "stage": "tensor-core"
    },
    {
      "text": "8. Partial sums accumulate in the VGPR register file across K. Steps 6-8 repeat along K.",
      "focus": ["register-file"],
      "dot": "register-file",
      "drill": "cu-detail",
      "stage": "accumulate"
    },
    {
      "text": "9. Epilogue: results move to vector ALUs, which add bias, apply activation, and quantize.",
      "focus": ["vector-alu", "wavefront-scheduler"],
      "dot": "vector-alu",
      "drill": "cu-detail",
      "stage": "epilogue"
    },
    {
      "text": "10. Results write back to HBM through the IOD; with tensor parallelism, xGMI all-reduces with the other 7 GPUs.",
      "focus": ["xgmi-link"],
      "dot": "xgmi-link",
      "drill": null,
      "stage": "writeback"
    }
  ],
